// Difficulty profiles (A13). Chosen at the start of a game and never changed
// afterwards: it changes the simulation, so it travels in the replay's header
// and goes into the state hash.
//
// Born with a single knob: phases 13, 14 and 16 add theirs here without
// touching the header or World::new's signature again.
(
    profiles: [
        // The residents of a newly-built house.
        //
        // At "easy" it is the whole capacity of a level-1 house, which is M0's
        // behaviour. At "hard" it is zero: the house only fills up by
        // migration (phase 15), and the city has to be earned. Validation
        // refuses anything beyond rules.residents_per_house_level[0] — a house
        // born beyond its own capacity is a state the game cannot represent.
        (id: "easy",   starting_residents_per_house: 4),
        (id: "normal", starting_residents_per_house: 2),
        (id: "hard",   starting_residents_per_house: 0),
    ],
)
